Activate a virtual environment:
source venv/bin/activate

Install dependencies:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Run the bot:
python main.py

Run with Docker Compose:
docker compose up -d --build

View logs:
docker compose logs -f bot

View proxy downloader debug:
tail -f logs/proxy_bot_downloader.log

Proxy fallback auto-joins Telegram sponsor channels shown by the proxy bot by default.
Disable it with:
PROXY_AUTO_JOIN_SPONSORS=false docker compose up -d

Run another environment:
APP_ENV=dev docker compose up -d --build

Instagram and TikTok photo posts are rendered as one MP4. Each photo is
shown once for 4 seconds, in the original post order. Total duration is
4 seconds multiplied by the number of photos. During the final 0.4 seconds
of each slot, the next photo slides in from the right with easing. Static
parts use sparse frames instead of encoding 30 identical frames per second;
transitions retain 30 fps. Original audio is included
when available: long tracks are trimmed with a short fade at the end;
short tracks finish naturally while the remaining photos continue.
Posts without available audio become silent videos. Photo albums received
from the fallback downloader are assembled the same way.
